%% showcase: Flowchart v11 shapes
%% prose: Every shape name in mermaid's v11 `@{ shape: … }` syntax renders. Where the scene has no outline of its own, the nearest one stands in, so a diagram keeps every node and its label.
%% approx: Cylinder for datastore and lin-cyl; cloud for bang; folded note for notch-rect (card) and tag-rect.
%% approx: Doubled sides (subroutine) for lin-rect, div-rect, win-pane and st-rect (processes).
%% approx: Hexagon for hourglass (collate); pill for delay; a plain box for curv-trap (display), as for odd.
%% approx: Trapezoid for tri (extract), flip-tri, notch-pent (loop-limit) and sl-rect (manual-input); trap-t and lean-l draw like trap-b and lean-r.
%% approx: Wavy document for docs, tag-doc, lin-doc and flag (paper-tape); horizontal cylinder for bow-rect (stored-data).
%% approx: Parallelogram for bolt; plain circle for cross-circ and dbl-circ; brace, brace-r and braces show just their text.
%% approx: Icon and image nodes (icon:, img:) are drawn as their label, or the icon name, in a box of their form.
